GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the amount the court allowed from all the sums together within the limit` IS
    `s 2(3) the amount the court allows from the sums taken together is within the limit` (`my contract from what I know` `my contract has become impossible to perform or been otherwise frustrated` `the parties have been discharged from performing my contract any further` `the date the parties were discharged` FALSE `my contract is a charterparty` `my charterparty is a time charterparty` `my charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise` `my contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` `my contract is a contract of insurance` `section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract` `my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods` `my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished`) (`my sums taken together` `the total of the sums I paid` `the total of the sums I still had to pay` `every sum I have counted was paid or payable in pursuance of the contract before the parties were discharged`) (`Expenses facts` OF `expenses were incurred before the parties were discharged in, or for the purpose of, performing the contract`, `the amount of those expenses`, `the sum the court includes for overhead expenses`, `the sum the court includes for work or services performed personally`) `the amount the court allows`

-- s 2(2) and (3).  The whole sum paid, less whatever the court allows the other party to keep.  If the court does not consider it just to allow anything, or no expenses were incurred, the whole sum.
-- NOTHING while the court has not said how much it allows.
-- Not asked (fixed placeholders; no rule this question reaches reads them): the Government is a party to my contract = FALSE; the date my contract was made = 1 January 2000.
@export How much of the money I paid can I get back once the court has allowed the other party to keep part of it (s 2(2) and (3))?
GIVEN `my contract has become impossible to perform or been otherwise frustrated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your contract become impossible to perform, or been otherwise frustrated?
      `the parties have been discharged from performing my contract any further` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the parties to your contract been discharged from performing it any further because of that?
      `the date the parties were discharged` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the parties discharged from performing the contract any further? (If they have not been discharged, give any date: it is not used.)
      `my contract is a charterparty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a charterparty?
