      `my contract is a contract of insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a contract of insurance?
      `section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 apply to your contract? (That section avoids a contract for the sale of specific goods which perish before the risk has passed to the buyer.)
      `my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods?
      `my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract frustrated because the goods have perished?
      `the amount of the sum` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the sum, in dollars?
      `the sum was paid or payable in pursuance of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the sum paid, or payable, in pursuance of the contract?
      `the sum was paid or fell payable before the parties were discharged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the sum paid, or did it fall payable, before the parties were discharged? (The Act says "before the time"; if it was on the very day of the discharge, answer according to which came first.)
      `expenses were incurred before the parties were discharged in, or for the purpose of, performing the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the party who received the sum, or was to receive it, incur expenses before the parties were discharged in, or for the purpose of, performing the contract?
      `the amount of those expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of those expenses, in dollars? (0 if none)
      `the sum the court includes for overhead expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc What sum, in dollars, has the court included for overhead expenses? (0 if none)
      `the sum the court includes for work or services performed personally` IS A NUMBER @desc What sum, in dollars, has the court included for work or services performed personally by that party? (0 if none)
      `the court considers it just to allow the party to retain or recover the sum` IS A `My answer` @desc Does the court consider it just, having regard to all the circumstances of the case, to allow the party to retain or recover the sum? (Choose I am not sure if the court has not yet decided.)
      `the court has decided how much to allow` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court decided how much to allow the party to retain or recover?
      `the amount the court allows` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in dollars, has the court allowed? (0 if it has not decided or allowed nothing)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of the money I paid can I get back` IS
    `s 2(2) subject to s 2(3) the amount of the sum paid that is recoverable` (`my contract from what I know` `my contract has become impossible to perform or been otherwise frustrated` `the parties have been discharged from performing my contract any further` `the date the parties were discharged` FALSE `my contract is a charterparty` `my charterparty is a time charterparty` `my charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise` `my contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` `my contract is a contract of insurance` `section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract` `my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods` `my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished`) (`Sum facts` OF `the amount of the sum`, TRUE, `the sum was paid or payable in pursuance of the contract`, `the sum was paid or fell payable before the parties were discharged`) (`Expenses facts` OF `expenses were incurred before the parties were discharged in, or for the purpose of, performing the contract`, `the amount of those expenses`, `the sum the court includes for overhead expenses`, `the sum the court includes for work or services performed personally`) (`what I say, as a fact` `the court considers it just to allow the party to retain or recover the sum`) (`my amount if the court has decided` `the court has decided how much to allow` `the amount the court allows`)

