DECIDE `How much of a sum I was to pay remains payable` IS
    `s 2(2) subject to s 2(3) the amount of the sum payable that remains payable` (`my contract from what I know` `my contract has become impossible to perform or been otherwise frustrated` `the parties have been discharged from performing my contract any further` `the date the parties were discharged` FALSE `my contract is a charterparty` `my charterparty is a time charterparty` `my charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise` `my contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` `my contract is a contract of insurance` `section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract` `my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods` `my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished`) (`Sum facts` OF `the amount of the sum`, FALSE, `the sum was paid or payable in pursuance of the contract`, `the sum was paid or fell payable before the parties were discharged`) (`Expenses facts` OF `expenses were incurred before the parties were discharged in, or for the purpose of, performing the contract`, `the amount of those expenses`, `the sum the court includes for overhead expenses`, `the sum the court includes for work or services performed personally`) (`what I say, as a fact` `the court considers it just to allow the party to retain or recover the sum`) (`my amount if the court has decided` `the court has decided how much to allow` `the amount the court allows`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `A valuable benefit (s 2(4))`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 2(4).  Where a party obtained a valuable benefit, other than a payment of money to which s 2(2) applies, before the discharge, by reason of what the other party did in performing the contract,
-- a sum (if any) is recoverable from them as the court considers just.  How much is the court's judgment.
-- Not asked (fixed placeholders; no rule this question reaches reads them): the Government is a party to my contract = FALSE; the value of the benefit to the party who obtained it = 0; the sums retained = 0; the date my contract was made = 1 January 2000.
@export Can a sum be recovered from the party who obtained a valuable benefit from what the other party did under the contract (s 2(4))?
GIVEN `my contract has become impossible to perform or been otherwise frustrated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your contract become impossible to perform, or been otherwise frustrated?
      `the parties have been discharged from performing my contract any further` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the parties to your contract been discharged from performing it any further because of that?
      `the date the parties were discharged` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the parties discharged from performing the contract any further? (If they have not been discharged, give any date: it is not used.)
      `my contract is a charterparty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a charterparty?
      `my charterparty is a time charterparty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your contract is a charterparty, is it a time charterparty? (Answer No if it is not a charterparty.)
      `my charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your contract is a charterparty, is it a charterparty by way of demise? (Answer No if it is not a charterparty.)
      `my contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a contract for the carriage of goods by sea?
      `my contract is a contract of insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a contract of insurance?
      `section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 apply to your contract? (That section avoids a contract for the sale of specific goods which perish before the risk has passed to the buyer.)
      `my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods?
      `my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract frustrated because the goods have perished?
      `a party has obtained a valuable benefit from what the other party did under the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a party to the contract obtained a valuable benefit by reason of anything the other party did in, or for the purpose of, performing the contract?
      `the benefit was obtained before the parties were discharged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the benefit obtained before the parties were discharged? (The Act says "before the time"; if it was on the very day of the discharge, answer according to which came first.)
      `the benefit is a payment of money to which section 2(2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the benefit a payment of money that was paid, or payable, under the contract before the parties were discharged?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a sum be recovered for a valuable benefit` IS
    `s 2(4) a sum is recoverable from the party who obtained a valuable benefit` (`my contract from what I know` `my contract has become impossible to perform or been otherwise frustrated` `the parties have been discharged from performing my contract any further` `the date the parties were discharged` FALSE `my contract is a charterparty` `my charterparty is a time charterparty` `my charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise` `my contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` `my contract is a contract of insurance` `section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract` `my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods` `my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished`) (`Benefit facts` OF `a party has obtained a valuable benefit from what the other party did under the contract`, `the benefit was obtained before the parties were discharged`, `the benefit is a payment of money to which section 2(2) applies`, 0, 0)

-- s 2(4).  Not more than the value of the benefit to the party who obtained it.
-- Not asked (fixed placeholders; no rule this question reaches reads them): the Government is a party to my contract = FALSE; the sums retained = 0; the date my contract was made = 1 January 2000.
@export What is the most that can be recovered for the valuable benefit (s 2(4))?
GIVEN `my contract has become impossible to perform or been otherwise frustrated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your contract become impossible to perform, or been otherwise frustrated?
      `the parties have been discharged from performing my contract any further` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the parties to your contract been discharged from performing it any further because of that?
      `the date the parties were discharged` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the parties discharged from performing the contract any further? (If they have not been discharged, give any date: it is not used.)
      `my contract is a charterparty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a charterparty?
      `my charterparty is a time charterparty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your contract is a charterparty, is it a time charterparty? (Answer No if it is not a charterparty.)
      `my charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your contract is a charterparty, is it a charterparty by way of demise? (Answer No if it is not a charterparty.)
      `my contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a contract for the carriage of goods by sea?
      `my contract is a contract of insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a contract of insurance?
      `section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 apply to your contract? (That section avoids a contract for the sale of specific goods which perish before the risk has passed to the buyer.)
      `my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods?
      `my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract frustrated because the goods have perished?
      `a party has obtained a valuable benefit from what the other party did under the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a party to the contract obtained a valuable benefit by reason of anything the other party did in, or for the purpose of, performing the contract?
      `the benefit was obtained before the parties were discharged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the benefit obtained before the parties were discharged? (The Act says "before the time"; if it was on the very day of the discharge, answer according to which came first.)
      `the benefit is a payment of money to which section 2(2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the benefit a payment of money that was paid, or payable, under the contract before the parties were discharged?
      `the value of the benefit to the party who obtained it` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the benefit, in dollars, to the party who obtained it?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most that can be recovered for the benefit` IS
    `s 2(4) the most that is recoverable for the valuable benefit` (`my contract from what I know` `my contract has become impossible to perform or been otherwise frustrated` `the parties have been discharged from performing my contract any further` `the date the parties were discharged` FALSE `my contract is a charterparty` `my charterparty is a time charterparty` `my charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise` `my contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` `my contract is a contract of insurance` `section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract` `my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods` `my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished`) (`Benefit facts` OF `a party has obtained a valuable benefit from what the other party did under the contract`, `the benefit was obtained before the parties were discharged`, `the benefit is a payment of money to which section 2(2) applies`, `the value of the benefit to the party who obtained it`, 0)

-- s 2(4).  The sum must not exceed the value of the benefit to the party who obtained it.
-- Not asked (fixed placeholders; no rule this question reaches reads them): the Government is a party to my contract = FALSE; the sums retained = 0; the date my contract was made = 1 January 2000.
@export Is the sum the court considers just within the limit the Act sets for a valuable benefit (s 2(4))?
GIVEN `my contract has become impossible to perform or been otherwise frustrated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your contract become impossible to perform, or been otherwise frustrated?
      `the parties have been discharged from performing my contract any further` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the parties to your contract been discharged from performing it any further because of that?
      `the date the parties were discharged` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the parties discharged from performing the contract any further? (If they have not been discharged, give any date: it is not used.)
      `my contract is a charterparty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a charterparty?
      `my charterparty is a time charterparty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your contract is a charterparty, is it a time charterparty? (Answer No if it is not a charterparty.)
