GIVEN `expenses were incurred before the parties were discharged in, or for the purpose of, performing the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the party who received the sum, or was to receive it, incur expenses before the parties were discharged in, or for the purpose of, performing the contract?
      `the amount of those expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of those expenses, in dollars? (0 if none)
      `the sum the court includes for overhead expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc What sum, in dollars, has the court included for overhead expenses? (0 if none)
      `the sum the court includes for work or services performed personally` IS A NUMBER @desc What sum, in dollars, has the court included for work or services performed personally by that party? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What are the expenses as the court estimates them` IS
    `s 2(5) the expenses as estimated` (`Expenses facts` OF `expenses were incurred before the parties were discharged in, or for the purpose of, performing the contract`, `the amount of those expenses`, `the sum the court includes for overhead expenses`, `the sum the court includes for work or services performed personally`)

-- s 2(5).  In estimating the expenses incurred by a party, the court may include a reasonable sum for overhead expenses and for work or services that party performed personally.
