-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Insurance money (s 2(6))`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 2(6).  In considering whether any sum ought to be recovered or retained under section 2, the court shall not take into account insurance money that became payable to that party because of the frustration,
-- unless there was an obligation to insure imposed by an express term of the frustrated contract or by or under any enactment.  Yes: it must leave it out.  No: the exception applies, so the bar does not.  NOTHING: other sums, or the Act does not say.
@export Must the court leave out of account insurance money that has become payable to a party because of the frustration (s 2(6))?
GIVEN `the court is considering whether any sum ought to be recovered or retained under section 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court considering whether any sum ought to be recovered or retained under section 2 by that party?
      `insurance money has become payable to that party because of the frustration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has money become payable to that party under a contract of insurance because of the circumstances that frustrated the contract?
      `an express term of my contract required insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did an express term of the frustrated contract oblige a party to insure?
      `a law required insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there an obligation to insure imposed by or under any enactment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the court leave insurance money out of account` IS
    `s 2(6) the court shall not take the insurance sums into account` (`Insurance facts` OF `the court is considering whether any sum ought to be recovered or retained under section 2`, `insurance money has become payable to that party because of the frustration`, `an express term of my contract required insurance`, `a law required insurance`)

-- s 2(6).  No where the bar applies.  NOTHING where the exception applies (the Act lifts the bar but does not itself say the court may count the money) or the sums are not within the bar.
@export May the court take that insurance money into account (s 2(6))?
GIVEN `the court is considering whether any sum ought to be recovered or retained under section 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court considering whether any sum ought to be recovered or retained under section 2 by that party?
      `insurance money has become payable to that party because of the frustration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has money become payable to that party under a contract of insurance because of the circumstances that frustrated the contract?
      `an express term of my contract required insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did an express term of the frustrated contract oblige a party to insure?
      `a law required insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there an obligation to insure imposed by or under any enactment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court take insurance money into account` IS
    `s 2(6) the court may take the insurance sums into account` (`Insurance facts` OF `the court is considering whether any sum ought to be recovered or retained under section 2`, `insurance money has become payable to that party because of the frustration`, `an express term of my contract required insurance`, `a law required insurance`)

