§§ `A benefit given to someone else (s 2(7))`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 2(7).  Where a person took on obligations in return for a benefit that another party conferred on someone else (a party or not),
-- the court may, if it considers it just, treat that benefit, for s 2(4), as obtained by the person who took on the obligations.
-- Not asked (fixed placeholders; no rule this question reaches reads them): the Government is a party to my contract = FALSE; the date my contract was made = 1 January 2000.
