      `the parties have been discharged from performing my contract any further` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the parties to your contract been discharged from performing it any further because of that?
      `the date the parties were discharged` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the parties discharged from performing the contract any further? (If they have not been discharged, give any date: it is not used.)
      `my contract is a charterparty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a charterparty?
      `my charterparty is a time charterparty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your contract is a charterparty, is it a time charterparty? (Answer No if it is not a charterparty.)
      `my charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your contract is a charterparty, is it a charterparty by way of demise? (Answer No if it is not a charterparty.)
      `my contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a contract for the carriage of goods by sea?
      `my contract is a contract of insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a contract of insurance?
      `section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 apply to your contract? (That section avoids a contract for the sale of specific goods which perish before the risk has passed to the buyer.)
      `my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods?
      `my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract frustrated because the goods have perished?
      `a person has assumed obligations under the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a person assumed obligations under the contract?
      `the obligations were assumed in consideration of a benefit conferred by another party upon another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were those obligations assumed in consideration of the conferring of a benefit by another party to the contract upon another person?
      `the person who received the benefit is a party to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who received that benefit a party to the contract? (The Act applies whether or not they are.)
      `the court considers it just to treat the benefit as obtained by the person who assumed the obligations` IS A `My answer` @desc Does the court consider it just, in all the circumstances of the case, to treat the benefit as obtained by the person who assumed the obligations? (Choose I am not sure if the court has not yet decided.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court treat the benefit as obtained by the person who took on the obligations` IS
    `s 2(7) the court may treat the benefit conferred on another person as a benefit obtained by the person who assumed the obligations` (`my contract from what I know` `my contract has become impossible to perform or been otherwise frustrated` `the parties have been discharged from performing my contract any further` `the date the parties were discharged` FALSE `my contract is a charterparty` `my charterparty is a time charterparty` `my charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise` `my contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` `my contract is a contract of insurance` `section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract` `my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods` `my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished`) (`Obligor facts` OF `a person has assumed obligations under the contract`, `the obligations were assumed in consideration of a benefit conferred by another party upon another person`, `the person who received the benefit is a party to the contract`) (`what I say, as a fact` `the court considers it just to treat the benefit as obtained by the person who assumed the obligations`)

