    `s 3 this Act applies to the contract` (`my contract from what I know` TRUE `the parties have been discharged from performing my contract any further` `the date the parties were discharged` FALSE `my contract is a charterparty` `my charterparty is a time charterparty` `my charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise` `my contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` `my contract is a contract of insurance` `section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract` `my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods` `my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished`)

-- s 3(1).  The Act applies where the time of discharge is on or after 1 January 1959, and not where it is before.
-- Not asked (fixed placeholders; no rule this question reaches reads them): my contract has become impossible to perform or been otherwise frustrated = TRUE; the Government is a party to my contract = FALSE; my contract is a charterparty = FALSE; my charterparty is a time charterparty = FALSE; my charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise = FALSE; my contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea = FALSE; my contract is a contract of insurance = FALSE; section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract = FALSE; my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods = FALSE; my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished = FALSE; the date my contract was made = 1 January 2000.
