GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act apply to my Government contract in the same way` IS
    `s 3(2) this Act applies in like manner to a contract to which the Government is a party` (`my contract from what I know` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2000) `the Government is a party to my contract` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `My contract's own terms, and a part already performed (s 3(3) and (4))`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 3(3).  Where the contract is one the Act applies to and contains a provision meant to have effect if circumstances arise that frustrate the contract, or whether or not they arise,
-- the court shall give effect to that provision.  No if the contract has no such provision or the Act does not apply.
-- Not asked (fixed placeholders; no rule this question reaches reads them): my contract has become impossible to perform or been otherwise frustrated = TRUE; the Government is a party to my contract = FALSE; the date my contract was made = 1 January 2000.
@export Must the court give effect to my contract's own provision about frustration (s 3(3))?
GIVEN `the parties have been discharged from performing my contract any further` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the parties to your contract been discharged from performing it any further because of that?
      `the date the parties were discharged` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the parties discharged from performing the contract any further? (If they have not been discharged, give any date: it is not used.)
      `my contract is a charterparty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a charterparty?
      `my charterparty is a time charterparty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your contract is a charterparty, is it a time charterparty? (Answer No if it is not a charterparty.)
      `my charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your contract is a charterparty, is it a charterparty by way of demise? (Answer No if it is not a charterparty.)
      `my contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a contract for the carriage of goods by sea?
      `my contract is a contract of insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a contract of insurance?
      `section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 apply to your contract? (That section avoids a contract for the sale of specific goods which perish before the risk has passed to the buyer.)
      `my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods?
      `my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract frustrated because the goods have perished?
      `my contract has a provision for the event of frustration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your contract contain a provision which, on its true construction, is meant to have effect if circumstances arise that frustrate the contract (or would, but for that provision)?
      `my contract has a provision that has effect whether or not frustration arises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your contract contain a provision which, on its true construction, is meant to have effect whether or not such circumstances arise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the court give effect to my contract's own provision` IS
    `s 3(3) the court is to give effect to the provision of the contract` (`my contract from what I know` TRUE `the parties have been discharged from performing my contract any further` `the date the parties were discharged` FALSE `my contract is a charterparty` `my charterparty is a time charterparty` `my charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise` `my contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` `my contract is a contract of insurance` `section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract` `my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods` `my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished`) (`Contract provision facts` OF `my contract has a provision for the event of frustration`, `my contract has a provision that has effect whether or not frustration arises`)

-- s 3(3).  Section 2 is given effect only to the extent, if any, that appears to the court consistent with the contract's own provision, and never beyond what section 2 would give.
-- NOTHING while the court has not said how much is consistent, or where the contract has no such provision.
-- Not asked (fixed placeholders; no rule this question reaches reads them): my contract has become impossible to perform or been otherwise frustrated = TRUE; the Government is a party to my contract = FALSE; the date my contract was made = 1 January 2000.
@export How much of the adjustment section 2 would give is given effect, now that my contract has its own provision (s 3(3))?
GIVEN `the parties have been discharged from performing my contract any further` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the parties to your contract been discharged from performing it any further because of that?
      `the date the parties were discharged` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the parties discharged from performing the contract any further? (If they have not been discharged, give any date: it is not used.)
      `my contract is a charterparty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a charterparty?
      `my charterparty is a time charterparty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your contract is a charterparty, is it a time charterparty? (Answer No if it is not a charterparty.)
      `my charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your contract is a charterparty, is it a charterparty by way of demise? (Answer No if it is not a charterparty.)
      `my contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a contract for the carriage of goods by sea?
      `my contract is a contract of insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a contract of insurance?
      `section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 apply to your contract? (That section avoids a contract for the sale of specific goods which perish before the risk has passed to the buyer.)
      `my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods?
      `my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract frustrated because the goods have perished?
      `my contract has a provision for the event of frustration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your contract contain a provision which, on its true construction, is meant to have effect if circumstances arise that frustrate the contract (or would, but for that provision)?
      `my contract has a provision that has effect whether or not frustration arises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your contract contain a provision which, on its true construction, is meant to have effect whether or not such circumstances arise?
      `the amount section 2 would otherwise give effect to` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in dollars, would section 2 otherwise give effect to?
      `the court has said what is consistent with the provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court said how much of the section 2 adjustment appears to it to be consistent with the provision?
      `the amount the court finds consistent with the provision` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in dollars, of the section 2 adjustment does the court find consistent with the provision? (0 if it has not said, or if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of section 2 is given effect` IS
    `s 3(3) the amount of section 2 that is given effect` (`my contract from what I know` TRUE `the parties have been discharged from performing my contract any further` `the date the parties were discharged` FALSE `my contract is a charterparty` `my charterparty is a time charterparty` `my charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise` `my contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` `my contract is a contract of insurance` `section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract` `my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods` `my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished`) (`Contract provision facts` OF `my contract has a provision for the event of frustration`, `my contract has a provision that has effect whether or not frustration arises`) `the amount section 2 would otherwise give effect to` (`my amount if the court has decided` `the court has said what is consistent with the provision` `the amount the court finds consistent with the provision`)

-- s 3(4).  Where it appears to the court that a part of the contract can properly be severed, being a part wholly performed before the discharge (or performed but for the payment of sums that are or can be ascertained),
-- the court shall treat that part as a separate contract that was not frustrated.
-- Not asked (fixed placeholders; no rule this question reaches reads them): my contract has become impossible to perform or been otherwise frustrated = TRUE; the Government is a party to my contract = FALSE; the date my contract was made = 1 January 2000.
@export Must the court treat a part of my contract that was already performed as a separate contract that was not frustrated (s 3(4))?
GIVEN `the parties have been discharged from performing my contract any further` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the parties to your contract been discharged from performing it any further because of that?
      `the date the parties were discharged` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the parties discharged from performing the contract any further? (If they have not been discharged, give any date: it is not used.)
      `my contract is a charterparty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a charterparty?
      `my charterparty is a time charterparty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your contract is a charterparty, is it a time charterparty? (Answer No if it is not a charterparty.)
      `my charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your contract is a charterparty, is it a charterparty by way of demise? (Answer No if it is not a charterparty.)
      `my contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a contract for the carriage of goods by sea?
      `my contract is a contract of insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a contract of insurance?
      `section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 apply to your contract? (That section avoids a contract for the sale of specific goods which perish before the risk has passed to the buyer.)
      `my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods?
      `my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract frustrated because the goods have perished?
      `it appears to the court that a part of my contract can properly be severed` IS A `My answer` @desc Does it appear to the court that a part of the contract can properly be severed from the remainder? (Choose I am not sure if the court has not yet said.)
      `that part was wholly performed before the parties were discharged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that part wholly performed before the parties were discharged?
      `that part was performed except for payment of sums that are or can be ascertained under the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that part performed except for the payment, in respect of that part, of sums which are or can be ascertained under the contract?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the court treat a performed part as a separate contract` IS
    `s 3(4) the court is to treat the part of the contract as a separate contract that has not been frustrated` (`my contract from what I know` TRUE `the parties have been discharged from performing my contract any further` `the date the parties were discharged` FALSE `my contract is a charterparty` `my charterparty is a time charterparty` `my charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise` `my contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` `my contract is a contract of insurance` `section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract` `my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods` `my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished`) (`Severable part facts` OF (`what I say, as a fact` `it appears to the court that a part of my contract can properly be severed`), `that part was wholly performed before the parties were discharged`, `that part was performed except for payment of sums that are or can be ascertained under the contract`)

-- s 3(4).  Where the severance rule applies, section 2 applies only to the remainder, not to the severed part.  NOTHING where it does not apply: s 3(4) then says nothing about either portion.
-- Not asked (fixed placeholders; no rule this question reaches reads them): my contract has become impossible to perform or been otherwise frustrated = TRUE; the Government is a party to my contract = FALSE; the date my contract was made = 1 January 2000.
@export Does section 2 apply to this portion of my contract (s 3(4))?
GIVEN `the parties have been discharged from performing my contract any further` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the parties to your contract been discharged from performing it any further because of that?
      `the date the parties were discharged` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the parties discharged from performing the contract any further? (If they have not been discharged, give any date: it is not used.)
      `my contract is a charterparty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a charterparty?
      `my charterparty is a time charterparty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your contract is a charterparty, is it a time charterparty? (Answer No if it is not a charterparty.)
      `my charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your contract is a charterparty, is it a charterparty by way of demise? (Answer No if it is not a charterparty.)
      `my contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a contract for the carriage of goods by sea?
      `my contract is a contract of insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a contract of insurance?
      `section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 apply to your contract? (That section avoids a contract for the sale of specific goods which perish before the risk has passed to the buyer.)
      `my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods?
      `my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract frustrated because the goods have perished?
      `it appears to the court that a part of my contract can properly be severed` IS A `My answer` @desc Does it appear to the court that a part of the contract can properly be severed from the remainder? (Choose I am not sure if the court has not yet said.)
      `that part was wholly performed before the parties were discharged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that part wholly performed before the parties were discharged?
      `that part was performed except for payment of sums that are or can be ascertained under the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that part performed except for the payment, in respect of that part, of sums which are or can be ascertained under the contract?
      `the portion of my contract I ask about` IS A `The portion of my contract I ask about` @desc Are you asking about the part treated as a separate contract, or about the rest of your contract?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 2 apply to this portion of my contract` IS
    `s 3(4) section 2 applies to this portion of the contract` (`my contract from what I know` TRUE `the parties have been discharged from performing my contract any further` `the date the parties were discharged` FALSE `my contract is a charterparty` `my charterparty is a time charterparty` `my charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise` `my contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` `my contract is a contract of insurance` `section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract` `my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods` `my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished`) (`Severable part facts` OF (`what I say, as a fact` `it appears to the court that a part of my contract can properly be severed`), `that part was wholly performed before the parties were discharged`, `that part was performed except for payment of sums that are or can be ascertained under the contract`) (`the portion in the Act's terms` `the portion of my contract I ask about`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Am I outside the Act? (s 3(5))`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 3(5)(a).  The Act does not apply to a charterparty (except a time charterparty or a charterparty by way of demise) or to a contract, other than a charterparty, for the carriage of goods by sea.
-- Yes: outside the Act.  NOTHING: this paragraph does not catch your contract (a time or demise charterparty is excepted from the paragraph; the Act does not say more).
-- Not asked (fixed placeholders; no rule this question reaches reads them): my contract has become impossible to perform or been otherwise frustrated = TRUE; the parties have been discharged from performing my contract any further = TRUE; the date the parties were discharged = (Date 1 1 2000); the Government is a party to my contract = FALSE; my contract is a contract of insurance = FALSE; section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract = FALSE; my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods = FALSE; my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished = FALSE; the date my contract was made = 1 January 2000.
@export Is my contract outside the Act because it is a charterparty or a contract for the carriage of goods by sea (s 3(5)(a))? Yes means this paragraph takes your contract out of the Act. No answer ("not covered") means this paragraph does not take your contract out; that is so for a time charterparty and for a charterparty by way of demise, and it does not mean the Act is excluded. To find out whether the Act applies to your contract, ask "Does the Act apply to my contract (s 3)?"
GIVEN `my contract is a charterparty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a charterparty?
      `my charterparty is a time charterparty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your contract is a charterparty, is it a time charterparty? (Answer No if it is not a charterparty.)
      `my charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your contract is a charterparty, is it a charterparty by way of demise? (Answer No if it is not a charterparty.)
      `my contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a contract for the carriage of goods by sea?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I outside the Act as a charterparty or sea carriage` IS
    `s 3(5)(a) this Act shall not apply to the contract` (`my contract from what I know` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE `my contract is a charterparty` `my charterparty is a time charterparty` `my charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise` `my contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- s 3(5)(b).  The Act does not apply to a contract of insurance, except as section 2(6) provides.
-- Not asked (fixed placeholders; no rule this question reaches reads them): my contract has become impossible to perform or been otherwise frustrated = TRUE; the parties have been discharged from performing my contract any further = TRUE; the date the parties were discharged = (Date 1 1 2000); the Government is a party to my contract = FALSE; my contract is a charterparty = FALSE; my charterparty is a time charterparty = FALSE; my charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise = FALSE; my contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea = FALSE; section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract = FALSE; my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods = FALSE; my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished = FALSE; the date my contract was made = 1 January 2000.
@export Is my contract outside the Act because it is a contract of insurance (s 3(5)(b))? Yes means this paragraph takes your contract out of the Act (except as section 2(6) provides). No answer ("not covered") means this paragraph does not describe your contract; it does not mean the Act applies. To find out whether the Act applies to your contract, ask "Does the Act apply to my contract (s 3)?"
GIVEN `my contract is a contract of insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a contract of insurance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I outside the Act as an insurance contract` IS
    `s 3(5)(b) this Act shall not apply to the contract` (`my contract from what I know` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `my contract is a contract of insurance` FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- s 3(5)(b).  The exclusion of contracts of insurance is "except as is provided by section 2(6)": what section 2(6) provides still applies.
-- Not asked (fixed placeholders; no rule this question reaches reads them): my contract has become impossible to perform or been otherwise frustrated = TRUE; the parties have been discharged from performing my contract any further = TRUE; the date the parties were discharged = (Date 1 1 2000); the Government is a party to my contract = FALSE; my contract is a charterparty = FALSE; my charterparty is a time charterparty = FALSE; my charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise = FALSE; my contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea = FALSE; section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract = FALSE; my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods = FALSE; my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished = FALSE; the date my contract was made = 1 January 2000.
@export Does section 2(6) still apply although my contract is a contract of insurance (s 3(5)(b))?
GIVEN `my contract is a contract of insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract a contract of insurance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 2(6) still apply to my insurance contract` IS
    `s 3(5)(b) section 2(6) still applies although the contract is a contract of insurance` (`my contract from what I know` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `my contract is a contract of insurance` FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- s 3(5)(c).  The Act does not apply to a contract to which section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies, or to any other contract for the sale of specific goods where the contract is frustrated because the goods have perished.
-- Yes: outside the Act.  No: a contract for the sale of specific goods that has not been frustrated by their perishing.  NOTHING: not a sale of specific goods.
-- Not asked (fixed placeholders; no rule this question reaches reads them): my contract has become impossible to perform or been otherwise frustrated = TRUE; the parties have been discharged from performing my contract any further = TRUE; the date the parties were discharged = (Date 1 1 2000); the Government is a party to my contract = FALSE; my contract is a charterparty = FALSE; my charterparty is a time charterparty = FALSE; my charterparty is a charterparty by way of demise = FALSE; my contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea = FALSE; my contract is a contract of insurance = FALSE; the date my contract was made = 1 January 2000.
@export Is my contract outside the Act because it is a sale of specific goods that perished (s 3(5)(c))? Yes means this paragraph takes your contract out of the Act. No means it is a sale of specific goods that did not perish, so this paragraph does not take it out. No answer ("not covered") means this paragraph does not describe your contract; it does not mean the Act applies. To find out whether the Act applies to your contract, ask "Does the Act apply to my contract (s 3)?"
GIVEN `section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 apply to your contract? (That section avoids a contract for the sale of specific goods which perish before the risk has passed to the buyer.)
      `my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods?
      `my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract frustrated because the goods have perished?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I outside the Act as a sale of goods that perished` IS
    `s 3(5)(c) this Act shall not apply to the contract` (`my contract from what I know` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies to my contract` `my contract is for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods` `my contract is frustrated because the goods have perished`)
